# Standalone C++ reference-model build (make numerics-check).
#
# NOTE: model/vectors/*.vec and model/vectors/*.coeff are deliberately NOT
# ignored. Those files are committed source-of-truth golden vectors — the point
# of a golden vector is that a change to it appears as a reviewable diff — not
# build output. They are regenerated and compared, not rebuilt, by
# `make numerics-check` (issue #4) and `make coeff-check` (issue #10). See
# DECISIONS.md (issue #4 decision on the vector format, issue #10 decision 10).
model/cpp/build/

# Results are generated, never committed (dirs kept via .gitkeep).
# Note: pattern must not exclude the subdirectories themselves, or git cannot
# re-include the .gitkeep files beneath them.
results/*/*
# ... and loose files directly in results/, which `results/*/*` does not match.
# A calibration runner's own log lands there (issue #16), and PLAN.md standing
# rule 3 applies to it exactly as it does to everything one level deeper.
results/*.log
results/*.json
results/*.txt
!results/**/.gitkeep

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# Editor / OS noise
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Generated Verilator config package / headers (from config/*.json)
sim/verilator/generated/

# NOTE (issue #7): the generated register map is deliberately NOT ignored.
# rtl/control/generated/regmap_pkg.sv, model/cpp/regmap/regmap.hpp and
# docs/regmap.md are produced by scripts/gen_regmap.py from control/regmap.json
# and are committed, because a clean checkout must lint and simulate the control
# plane without running a generator first, and because a register-map change has
# to be reviewable as a diff. `make regmap-check` — a prerequisite of both
# `make lint` and `make sim-tiny` — fails if any of them differs from what the
# source of truth generates, so they cannot drift. The machine-readable
# results/regmap/regmap.json IS generated output and is covered by the
# results/*/* rule above. See DECISIONS.md (issue #7, decision 2).

# NOTE (issue #11): the generated FFT twiddle table is deliberately NOT ignored.
# rtl/fft/generated/fft_twiddle_pkg.sv and model/cpp/fft/fft_twiddle_table.hpp
# are produced by model/python/gen_fft_twiddles.py and are committed, for the two
# reasons the register map is — a clean checkout must lint and simulate without
# running a generator first, and a coefficient change has to be reviewable as a
# diff — plus one that is specific to them: they hold the only numbers in this
# design that come from transcendental functions, and computing those at
# elaboration time would mean Verilator's libm, Quartus's libm and Python's each
# producing their own table with nothing in the flow able to notice a
# disagreement. `make fft-check` — a prerequisite of both `make lint` and
# `make sim-tiny` — fails if either artefact differs from what the generator
# produces, so they cannot drift. model/vectors/fft64.vec is committed for the
# reason the other golden vectors are; see model/vectors/README.md and
# DECISIONS.md (issue #11).

# SPEC 18 calibration sweep working copies (scripts/run_calibration.py).
#
# Each point compiles in its own copy of quartus/calibration/, placed two levels
# below the repository root so the ../../rtl paths in the copied qsf still
# resolve. The copies are deleted after each point unless --keep-work is given;
# these patterns are the safety net, and they also cover a compile run by hand
# inside the tracked calibration project.
results/calib_*/
quartus/calibration/output_files/
quartus/calibration/qdb/
quartus/calibration/db/
quartus/calibration/dni/
quartus/calibration/incremental_db/
quartus/calibration/tmp-clearbox/
